concept_lookup_meta_recipe
  record_type meta_recipe
  topic live_concept_lookup
  issue 1138
  selector rust/src/seed/sources.rs
  walker rust/src/source_walk.rs
  extractor rust/src/concept_lookup.rs
  memory rust/src/concept_sense_ledger.rs
  consumer rust/src/coding/concept_discovery.rs
  consumer rust/src/solver.rs
  note "Five steps, in the order the kernel runs them: name the surfaces nobody has accounted for, let the registry say which sources may answer that kind of need, walk each one inside declared bounds, read whatever the bytes actually say, and remember the identity rather than the payload. Every function named here is checked to exist in the file named here by rust/tests/unit/specification/concept_lookup_meta_algorithm.rs, so the recipe is a claim about the live source and not a description of it."
concept_lookup_step_enumerate
  record_type meta_step
  order 1
  function unknown_surfaces
  source rust/src/concept_lookup.rs
  effect "Name every surface in the prompt that no seeded meaning, and no quoted example, accounts for."
concept_lookup_step_select
  record_type meta_step
  order 2
  function select_sources
  source rust/src/source_walk.rs
  effect "Ask the registry which sources declare they answer a concept need, in declared order, minus the ones the settings opted out and the ones this subject cannot bind."
concept_lookup_step_walk
  record_type meta_step
  order 3
  function walk_sources
  source rust/src/source_walk.rs
  effect "Capture each selected source inside the declared depth, page, service and staleness bounds, leaving an outcome row for every source that could have contributed."
concept_lookup_step_extract
  record_type meta_step
  order 4
  function lookup_surface
  source rust/src/concept_lookup.rs
  effect "Read the captured bytes with the extractor the registry binds to that source, and attach the exact provenance of those bytes to every sense."
concept_lookup_step_remember
  record_type meta_step
  order 5
  function remember
  source rust/src/concept_sense_ledger.rs
  effect "File the sense under a content id derived from the bytes, the headword and the gloss, so forgetting it costs nothing that the captures cannot re-derive."
